    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Peukert&#x27;s 1897 power law, t = C_p/I^k, says a lead-acid battery discharged faster delivers less total charge. Using effective_capacity, this example compares the ideal Peukert exponent k=1 (same capacity at every rate) with a realistic k=1.2, then draws discharge curves from ConstantCurrentBattery (a deliberately simplified model; see its docstring) whose runtimes shrink faster than 1/I.">

